CPIC database extract v1.60.0
==============================

Artifact: cpic-v1.60.0.json.gz
Source: https://files.cpicpgx.org/data/database/cpic_db_dump-v1.60.0.sql.gz
Release: https://github.com/cpicpgx/cpic-data/releases/tag/v1.60.0
Accessed: 2026-09-26
Source SHA-256: 1f02d87a492fffacb52a6d3ca5f45c5f7d6862bdfd382436d2cf7595b08d1ffe
Extract SHA-256: 47af59c170dc2e498a81237392f3ead4291856aa1f3805b60e57b7b3a4affd7f

This is a column-limited derived extract of nine CPIC COPY tables: drug,
guideline, pair, allele_definition, allele_location_value, sequence_location,
gene_result, gene_result_lookup, and gene_result_diplotype. The builder parses data blocks
only; it never executes the downloaded SQL. No recommendation text or patient
data is in this artifact.

The CPIC project makes its curated content available under CC0 1.0 and asks
for attribution and the version of database content used:
https://github.com/cpicpgx/cpic-data/blob/main/LICENSE.md
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/
CPIC database and API use is also subject to the terms linked in that LICENSE.
CPIC guidance changes; this extract is pinned to v1.60.0 and is not a current
clinical recommendation. CPIC is a registered service mark of HHS.

The local reader only maps externally confirmed diplotypes to an exact CPIC
phenotype. It does not call star alleles from array genotypes or issue drug
recommendations. The CDC GeT-RM consensus panel has not yet been validated
against this implementation.
